+      "content": "# Embedded execution qualification and timeout diagnostics\n\n## Scope and final source\n\nImplemented approved T4/T5 in exactly three source files:\n\n- `skills/adk-cmake-cross-build/SKILL.md`: 1.0.5 → 1.0.6, 4125 → 4709 bytes.\n- `skills/adk-integration-hil-sil/SKILL.md`: 1.0.3 → 1.0.4, 4318 → 3866 bytes.\n- `tests/test_skill_command_examples.py`: actual command examples, result-reader negatives and owned-process timeout checks.\n\nThe two Skill entries together add **132 bytes**. No profile cap, runtime/router, global version projection or unrelated source file was changed by this implementation owner. All seven existing SOP sections remain. The portfolio source audit covers all 25 assigned entries and all 16 shipped local references; 23 entries are retained with individual reasons.\n\n## Behavior\n\nCMake now selects preset/manual in one mutually exclusive block and shares its build/test invocation. Execution backends run CTest exactly once into a fresh report directory under the declared task evidence parent. A standard-library Python reader verifies the declared CTest JUnit format, rejects missing/malformed/unknown/failing results, counts actual completed passing cases, and rejects zero passes. Mixed pass/skip/disabled reports explicitly say `partial`; required-case identity remains a separate task requirement. Ordinary CTest failure exits remain unchanged. Compile-only does not read test-preset or evidence variables and does not require Python.\n\nHIL/SIL independently publishes a fresh report collection command and explains the corresponding result qualification. It does not require another Skill, duplicate the parser, hardcode `build/sil`, or claim that command exit zero automatically qualifies HIL/SIL.\n\nThe test helper starts a dedicated process group. A timeout terminates that owned group, retains both captured streams plus execution identity, and reports the original **15 second aggregate work budget** separately from a bounded cleanup allowance. CMake fixtures enable shell trace only inside tests, so a timeout shows the last attempted configure/build/test command. There is no automatic retry and no per-stage budget expansion.\n\n## Verification\n\n| Evidence | Observed result |\n|---|---|\n| `ctest-counterexamples/receipt.json` | Original manual block: valid all-skip fixture returns 0; actual JUnit has zero passing cases. Empty/all-disabled return 8 under CMake 3.31.6, preserving that negative result. |\n| `timeout-counterexample/receipt.json` | Original helper at actual default 15 seconds omits captured streams from its exception display and leaves a running descendant; controlled probe explicitly killed/reaped it. |\n| `verification/attempt2.json` and logs | 37 unittest methods: **32 passed, 5 skipped** because Ninja is absent. All eight new real Unix Makefiles/CMake/CTest cases ran. The original five Ninja/multiconfig cases still require Ninja and fail, rather than skip, when missing on GitHub Actions. |\n| `CtestReportReaderTests` within the preceding log | 15 positive/negative report scenarios: real-format success and partial results, all skipped/disabled/empty, wrong root, missing/unknown status, mismatched selected count, failure/error, invalid passing status, malformed/empty/missing XML. |\n| `verification/default-timeout-green/receipt.json` | Caller supplied no timeout override: work 15.019s, cleanup 0.002s, both streams displayed, child killed and explicitly reaped. Another process group's survival is separately covered by the real runner regression. |\n| `verification/content-regression-corrected.json` | Existing content, portfolio quality and trigger tests: **39 passed**. |\n| `verification/tool-identity.json` | Existing CMake/CTest 3.31.6 bytes match their stored wheel; executable/wheel SHA-256 values retained. No download or installation. |\n\nThe initial 37-method attempt had one fixture error: placing GNU make itself in a PATH directory containing spaces caused its recursive command to split that executable path. Only that fixture's tool-directory spelling was corrected to remove spaces; source and build directories still contain spaces. Independently, the process-state assertion was made tolerant of the child being reaped between existence/read, without accepting a running child. The failed attempt and both source fingerprints remain in `verification/attempt1.*` and `attempt2.*`.\n\nThe first direct content-test invocation omitted the repository's required `PYTHONPATH=src`, producing eight import errors. That invocation is retained as a harness setup error, not a Skill defect or RED result. Reading the existing shell wrappers established the required environment; the corrected invocation changed no source or expectations and passed all 39 tests.\n\n## Limits and handoff\n\nNinja/multiconfig and the original ADC strict-C90 CMake case are **not run locally** in this round and must execute in CI. The real native Make fixtures test command and report semantics only; they are not ARM builds, emulator/board execution or HIL evidence. No physical device, external inference API, model CLI or scheduled task was used.\n\nThe previous release runner's 15 second CMake timeout still has **unknown root cause**. The proven changes improve timeout observability and cleanup; the controlled sleep experiment does not establish why that historical CMake run timed out.\n\nIndependent source review, complete repository validation, original profile caps and remote CI/publication remain owned by root/reviewer. `implementation-receipt.json` binds final source hashes and the preserved raw evidence files for that handoff.\n"
